    ('pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000287', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'reading', 'reading-mcq-single', 'Multiple Choice, Single Answer', 'Sports Readiness', 'Read the text and answer the multiple-choice question by selecting the correct response. What should parents consider when introducing organized sports to their children?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Is the child interested in playing sports at all?"}, {"id": "B", "text": "Is the child at the right age or skill level for the sport?"}, {"id": "C", "text": "Does the child prefer team sports or private lessons?"}, {"id": "D", "text": "Does the child find the sport fun or too difficult?"}]'::jsonb, '["B"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single best answer.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Reading']::text[], TRUE, 0, 90, 'rp-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000287', 'g-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000287', 1, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000286', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'reading', 'reading-mcq-single', 'Multiple Choice, Single Answer', 'Knowledge', 'Read the text and answer the multiple-choice question by selecting the correct response. According to the author, what is the primary role of sources in academic writing?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Scholars should be careful to select reliable sources."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Scholars should use a wide variety of sources."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Sources should determine a scholarly argument."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Sources should serve as inspiration to scholars."}]'::jsonb, '["D"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single best answer.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Reading']::text[], TRUE, 0, 90, 'rp-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000286', 'g-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000286', 1, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000285', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'reading', 'reading-mcq-single', 'Multiple Choice, Single Answer', 'Persistence', 'Read the text and answer the multiple-choice question by selecting the correct response. Who participated as the subjects in the university study described in the passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Mothers from a wide range of backgrounds."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Mothers from rural areas."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Poorer mothers living in a city."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Mothers from wealthy families."}]'::jsonb, '["C"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single best answer.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Reading']::text[], TRUE, 0, 90, 'rp-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000285', 'g-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000285', 1, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000284', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'reading', 'reading-mcq-single', 'Multiple Choice, Single Answer', 'Human Development Index', 'Read the text and answer the multiple-choice question by selecting the correct response. Why is the UN Human Development Index considered a more rounded indicator than per capita GDP?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "It''s more official because it''s determined by an international inter-governmental organization."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Health is more important than purchasing power."}, {"id": "C", "text": "It Includes more than just economic factors in its evaluation including health and education."}, {"id": "D", "text": "It more accurately depicts the situation in countries like Niger and Norway."}]'::jsonb, '["C"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single best answer.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Reading']::text[], TRUE, 0, 90, 'rp-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000284', 'g-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000284', 1, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000283', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'reading', 'reading-mcq-single', 'Multiple Choice, Single Answer', 'Glaciers', 'Read the text and answer the multiple-choice question by selecting the correct response. At what intervals do surge glaciers move forward up to 100 times faster than usual?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "periods"}, {"id": "B", "text": "records"}, {"id": "C", "text": "speeds"}, {"id": "D", "text": "distances"}]'::jsonb, '["A"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single best answer.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Reading']::text[], TRUE, 0, 90, 'rp-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000283', 'g-pte-alfa-rmcsa-8000283', 1, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-swt-6000485', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'Design', 'Read the passage below and summarize it using one sentence. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the passage.', 'What is design? How can design be understood in a meaningful, holistic sense? It cannot simply be answered. Beyond all the
confusion created by the froth and bubble of advertising and publicity, beyond the visual pyrotechnics of virtuoso designers seeking
stardom, beyond the pronouncements of design gurus and the snake-oil salesmen of lifestyles, lies a simple truth. Design is one of
the basic characteristics of what it is to be human and an essential determinant of the quality of human life. It affects everyone in
every detail of every aspect of what they do throughout each day. As such, it matters profoundly. Very few aspects of the material
environment are incapable of improvement in some significant way by greater attention being paid to their design. Inadequate
lighting, machines that are not user-friendly, badly formatted information, are just a few examples of bad design that create
cumulative problems and tensions.
It is therefore worth asking: if these things are a necessary part of our existence, why are they often done so badly? There is no
simple answer. Cost factors are sometimes advanced in justification, but the margin between doing something well or badly can be
exceedingly small, and cost factors can in fact be reduced by appropriate design inputs. The use of the term ''appropriate'', however,
is an important qualification. The spectrum of capabilities covered by the term ''design'' requires that means be carefully adapted to
ends.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Write a single-sentence summary of 5-75 words covering key ideas.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Writing']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-swt-6000484', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'Financial Literacy Among Young Adults', 'Read the passage below and summarize it using one sentence. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the passage.', 'Ethan: Many young adults start earning money without understanding how to manage their income, control spending, or plan for
future financial responsibilities.
Grace: I agree, and some people rely heavily on credit cards or buy-now-pay-later services without fully understanding the interest,
fees, or consequences of missed payments.
Ethan: Poor financial decisions can lead to debt, stress, and difficulty achieving important goals, like buying a home or starting a
business.
Grace: That''s why financial literacy is important. People should understand budgeting, saving, borrowing, insurance, and basic
investing principles.
Ethan: Schools could introduce practical financial education to help students compare financial products, understand contracts, and
recognize potential scams.
Grace: Parents can also help by discussing household budgets and encouraging children to distinguish between essential expenses
and unnecessary purchases.
Ethan: Technology has made money management easier because budgeting apps let people track spending and monitor savings.
Grace: Yes, but people must protect their personal information and stay cautious about online investment schemes that promise
unrealistic returns.
Ethan: Governments and financial institutions could provide accessible educational resources, particularly for people who have
limited experience with banking or credit.
Grace: Ultimately, financial literacy helps people make informed decisions, reduce unnecessary debt, prepare for emergencies, and
build long-term financial security.
Ethan: I agree, because understanding money management helps not only high earners but anyone who wants to manage their
resources responsibly.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Write a single-sentence summary of 5-75 words covering key ideas.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Writing']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-swt-6000483', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'The Paradox of Technological Efficiency', 'Read the passage below and summarize it using one sentence. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the passage.', 'Technological advancement has traditionally been associated with greater efficiency, reduced labour requirements, and the
conservation of valuable resources. However, the assumption that improvements in efficiency inevitably lead to lower overall
consumption has increasingly been challenged by economists and environmental researchers. This apparent contradiction,
commonly described as the rebound effect, occurs when reductions in the cost of using a particular resource encourage greater
demand, potentially offsetting the benefits initially achieved through technological innovation.
Historically, the introduction of more efficient steam engines during the Industrial Revolution did not diminish coal consumption;
instead, their improved economic viability expanded industrial applications and ultimately increased aggregate demand. Similar
patterns can be observed in contemporary transportation systems, where fuel-efficient vehicles reduce the cost of travelling
individual distances but may simultaneously encourage longer journeys and more frequent vehicle use. Consequently, technological
improvements that appear environmentally beneficial at the individual level can produce substantially different outcomes when
examined across entire economies.
Nevertheless, the magnitude of such effects varies considerably according to consumer behaviour, market conditions, and
regulatory frameworks. Some researchers argue that efficiency improvements remain indispensable for sustainable development,
particularly when accompanied by policies that discourage excessive consumption. Others contend that technological innovation
alone cannot overcome the structural incentives driving continuous economic expansion. The central challenge, therefore, is not
merely to develop technologies that use fewer resources per unit of output, but to ensure that the economic and behavioural
responses they generate do not undermine their intended environmental benefits.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Write a single-sentence summary of 5-75 words covering key ideas.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Writing']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-swt-6000482', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'The Impact of Social Media', 'Read the passage below and summarize it using one sentence. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the passage.', 'Emma: Have you noticed how much time people spend on social media nowadays? Many people check their phones as soon as
they wake up.
James: Yes, social media has become a major part of everyday life. It allows people to communicate with friends and family, even
when they live in different countries.
Emma: It is also useful for businesses because they can promote their products, reach new customers, and communicate directly
with their audiences.
James: That''s true, and students can use social media to share educational resources, join discussion groups, and learn about
opportunities around the world.
Emma: However, I think excessive use can become a problem, especially when people spend hours comparing their lives with the
carefully selected images posted by others.
James: I agree. This can affect self-esteem and contribute to anxiety, particularly among young people who feel pressure to gain
likes and followers.
Emma: Another concern is the spread of misinformation. People sometimes share news without checking whether it comes from a
reliable source.
James: Exactly, and personal information can also be misused if users do not understand privacy settings or share too much online.
Emma: Do you think schools should teach students how to use social media responsibly?
James: Definitely. Digital literacy, fact-checking, privacy awareness, and sensible limits on screen time can help people benefit from
social media while reducing its negative effects.
Emma: So, the goal should not necessarily be to avoid social media completely, but to use it in a balanced and responsible way.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Write a single-sentence summary of 5-75 words covering key ideas.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Writing']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-swt-6000481', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'The Passing of Time', 'Read the passage below and summarize it using one sentence. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the passage.', 'The clock upon the silent wall counts moments lost beyond recall, while shadows stretch across the floor and daylight slips through
every door.
The seasons turn without a sound, as autumn leaves embrace the ground; The flowers bloom in early spring, then fade despite the
warmth they bring.
A child who plays beneath the sun believes the day has just begun, yet years will pass like drifting streams, and change the shape of
youthful dreams.
The mountains stand through wind and rain, while generations come again; the rivers carve the ancient stone, as time transforms
what once was known.
Some people chase a distant day, and let the present slip away; they dream of wealth or future fame, while simple pleasures stay
the same.
Others remember days gone by, and watch old memories multiply; They wish to walk familiar ground, where childhood laughter
once was found.
Yet time is neither foe nor friend; it marks beginnings and the end; no wealth can buy yesterday, nor can power make tomorrow stay.
So cherish what the present brings, the smallest joys, the simplest things; for life is not the years we keep, but moments held within
us deep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Write a single-sentence summary of 5-75 words covering key ideas.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Writing']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
