    ('pte-alfa-asq-5001995', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'speaking', 'pte-answer-short-question', 'Answer Short Questions', 'ASQ1995', 'You will hear a question. Please give a simple and short answer. Often just one or a few words is enough.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-b2064b93-afb8-4b7b-8bf4-b7fb2412952b.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'customer', 'Answer with one or a few words.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Speaking']::text[], TRUE, 3, 10, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-sst-13000701', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'summarize-spoken-text', 'Summarize Spoken Text', 'Children''s Life Quality', 'You will hear a short lecture. Write a summary for a fellow student who was not present at the lecture. You should write 50-70 words. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the lecture.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/c334719b-81ae-45a7-803c-4ca526bcdcb7.mp3', 'We have done a social science research on capacity of families and found this compelling and disturbing fact. The most disturbing
thing to me is that well-educated parents can always promise their children a prosperous future because these children have
sufficient educational capacity and support since they were born. The life chance of a child was set when they were five years old.
Well, this finding has been quite disturbing to me. And, I have to confess that currently there is no obvious way to address this deep
root of inequality in our society. Even public schools cannot completely offset the huge gaps brought by different family backgrounds
for vulnerable children. It reminds us that early-stage conditions play an enormous role in shaping the life chance of every individual.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'We have done a social science research on capacity of families and found this compelling and disturbing fact. The most disturbing
thing to me is that well-educated parents can always promise their children a prosperous future because these children have
sufficient educational capacity and support since they were born. The life chance of a child was set when they were five years old.
Well, this finding has been quite disturbing to me. And, I have to confess that currently there is no obvious way to address this deep
root of inequality in our society. Even public schools cannot completely offset the huge gaps brought by different family backgrounds
for vulnerable children. It reminds us that early-stage conditions play an enormous role in shaping the life chance of every individual.', 'Write a 50-70 word summary capturing key ideas of the spoken recording.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-sst-13000700', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'summarize-spoken-text', 'Summarize Spoken Text', 'Melatonin', 'You will hear a short lecture. Write a summary for a fellow student who was not present at the lecture. You should write 50-70 words. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the lecture.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-934e5c6b-14b3-4401-99f2-c899b1e85188.mp3', 'I''m just going to take on where we left off. The hormone I want to now talk about is called melatonin. The synthesis is in the pineal
gland, which is very small. It is the size of a pea in your brain. Descartes called it the "seat of the soul," and it is where melatonin is
made. It also has a rhythm. In a sense, it is the opposite of cortisol. It peaks at night. We call it the "darkness hormone." In every
species that we have studied, melatonin occurs at night. It is a hormone that prepares you for the things that your species does at
night. So, of course, in humans we sleep, but animals like rodents are awake. So, it is a hormone that is related to darkness
behavior.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'I''m just going to take on where we left off. The hormone I want to now talk about is called melatonin. The synthesis is in the pineal
gland, which is very small. It is the size of a pea in your brain. Descartes called it the "seat of the soul," and it is where melatonin is
made. It also has a rhythm. In a sense, it is the opposite of cortisol. It peaks at night. We call it the "darkness hormone." In every
species that we have studied, melatonin occurs at night. It is a hormone that prepares you for the things that your species does at
night. So, of course, in humans we sleep, but animals like rodents are awake. So, it is a hormone that is related to darkness
behavior.', 'Write a 50-70 word summary capturing key ideas of the spoken recording.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-sst-13000699', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'summarize-spoken-text', 'Summarize Spoken Text', 'Waste food', 'You will hear a short lecture. Write a summary for a fellow student who was not present at the lecture. You should write 50-70 words. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the lecture.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-1a013909-d968-4a50-9395-76d8774eb898.mp3', 'In the USA and in Oceania, which Australia is a part of, we''re not only the biggest wasters and losers of food in the world, but around
60% of it is at the consumption net, and when one drills down into what that 60% comprises, we find several things. One is that a lot
of food is wasted in supermarkets. We have an obsession with use-by dates, you know, you look at the product, and it says use by,
and once it hits that use-by date on the shelf, it has to come. You could have bought the same product the day before, and it''s in
your fridge a week or two later, and it''s still perfectly fine. Or an obsession with use-by dates is a contributing factor. The second one
comes around to what we purchase and how we use it, and there seems to be an attitude that, you know, food is a commodity, and
we''ve lost our respect for it. Oh, well, you know, I''ll buy that much. Oh well, I''ll buy a bit more. Not a good idea!', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In the USA and in Oceania, which Australia is a part of, we''re not only the biggest wasters and losers of food in the world, but around
60% of it is at the consumption net, and when one drills down into what that 60% comprises, we find several things. One is that a lot
of food is wasted in supermarkets. We have an obsession with use-by dates, you know, you look at the product, and it says use by,
and once it hits that use-by date on the shelf, it has to come. You could have bought the same product the day before, and it''s in
your fridge a week or two later, and it''s still perfectly fine. Or an obsession with use-by dates is a contributing factor. The second one
comes around to what we purchase and how we use it, and there seems to be an attitude that, you know, food is a commodity, and
we''ve lost our respect for it. Oh, well, you know, I''ll buy that much. Oh well, I''ll buy a bit more. Not a good idea!', 'Write a 50-70 word summary capturing key ideas of the spoken recording.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-sst-13000698', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'summarize-spoken-text', 'Summarize Spoken Text', 'Nuts', 'You will hear a short lecture. Write a summary for a fellow student who was not present at the lecture. You should write 50-70 words. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the lecture.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-8fea5b51-6756-48ba-8992-bccb2bfdde5f.mp3', 'You know, nut really fills you up. They are chewy. They are really great, great food, great protein, great minerals, and essential fats,
of course, and they fill you up, and they give you good nourishment, so they are a great snack. Instead of a chocolate bar, you get a
handful of nuts. Um, what I tell people about nuts, again, the general population coming into our place. Two-thirds of the people are
overweight or obese, so we have to have adequate calorie density. And that''s why the inclusion of grains and starches. But you also
have to deal with too much calorie density on the diet when people show up. So when we get the oils out of the diet, and when we
relegate foods like avocados, nuts and those types of things to when they appear in a dish. OK, so, you know, if I go get a black
bean wrap at a restaurant and has some avocado in it, that''s great. But if I buy a bag full of avocados and I go home and I start
putting them in my food, when I buy a bag of cashews or a bag of almonds, let''s take a nut we would all agree on is OK, a bag of
almonds, and I''m taking a handful of almonds. It''s very difficult for people to stay lean and keep their fat intake down when they''re
eating almonds.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'You know, nut really fills you up. They are chewy. They are really great, great food, great protein, great minerals, and essential fats,
of course, and they fill you up, and they give you good nourishment, so they are a great snack. Instead of a chocolate bar, you get a
handful of nuts. Um, what I tell people about nuts, again, the general population coming into our place. Two-thirds of the people are
overweight or obese, so we have to have adequate calorie density. And that''s why the inclusion of grains and starches. But you also
have to deal with too much calorie density on the diet when people show up. So when we get the oils out of the diet, and when we
relegate foods like avocados, nuts and those types of things to when they appear in a dish. OK, so, you know, if I go get a black
bean wrap at a restaurant and has some avocado in it, that''s great. But if I buy a bag full of avocados and I go home and I start
putting them in my food, when I buy a bag of cashews or a bag of almonds, let''s take a nut we would all agree on is OK, a bag of
almonds, and I''m taking a handful of almonds. It''s very difficult for people to stay lean and keep their fat intake down when they''re
eating almonds.', 'Write a 50-70 word summary capturing key ideas of the spoken recording.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-sst-13000697', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'summarize-spoken-text', 'Summarize Spoken Text', 'Andrew Carnegie', 'You will hear a short lecture. Write a summary for a fellow student who was not present at the lecture. You should write 50-70 words. You have 10 minutes to finish this task. Your response will be judged on the quality of your writing and on how well your response presents the key points in the lecture.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-ec23db30-5707-4fc2-9902-217ed5184295.mp3', 'Andrew Carnegie was born in Scotland in 1835. His family moved to America when he was 13 and settled in Pittsburgh. He found
jobs working in a fabric mill and a telegraph office. Carnegie always did well at whatever he set his mind to. He was known to make
improvements to any job he held. While working for the telegraph office, he began studying the railroad system, and he soon
became the superintendent. He took the money he had saved and invested it in an oil company. His investment return was good,
and then he went to England to learn how to make steel. He wanted to make steel that was cheaper and more durable than
American steel. He came back with his knowledge and built a huge steel factory. Carnegie''s Factory was very successful, and he
sold it for 480 million dollars. Carnegie was a very wealthy man, but he was more interested in philanthropy than spending his
money on himself. He spent the rest of his life giving his money away to worthy causes. Reading and learning were very important to
him, so he built many libraries. He also established universities and research institutes. Carnegie built hospitals, museums, and
theaters. One of the most recognizable buildings he built was Carnegie Hall in New York City. Carnegie Hall hosts many concerts
and symphonies each year and is an important part of New York City culture. Andrew Carnegie passed away at the age of 83. In his
lifetime, he gave away 90% of his fortune. He is known as a man who was selfless and wanted to do good for others.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Andrew Carnegie was born in Scotland in 1835. His family moved to America when he was 13 and settled in Pittsburgh. He found
jobs working in a fabric mill and a telegraph office. Carnegie always did well at whatever he set his mind to. He was known to make
improvements to any job he held. While working for the telegraph office, he began studying the railroad system, and he soon
became the superintendent. He took the money he had saved and invested it in an oil company. His investment return was good,
and then he went to England to learn how to make steel. He wanted to make steel that was cheaper and more durable than
American steel. He came back with his knowledge and built a huge steel factory. Carnegie''s Factory was very successful, and he
sold it for 480 million dollars. Carnegie was a very wealthy man, but he was more interested in philanthropy than spending his
money on himself. He spent the rest of his life giving his money away to worthy causes. Reading and learning were very important to
him, so he built many libraries. He also established universities and research institutes. Carnegie built hospitals, museums, and
theaters. One of the most recognizable buildings he built was Carnegie Hall in New York City. Carnegie Hall hosts many concerts
and symphonies each year and is an important part of New York City culture. Andrew Carnegie passed away at the age of 83. In his
lifetime, he gave away 90% of his fortune. He is known as a man who was selfless and wanted to do good for others.', 'Write a 50-70 word summary capturing key ideas of the spoken recording.', 'medium', 10, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 0, 600, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcma-14000228', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcma', 'MCQ Multiple Answer', 'Language Skills', 'According to the audio, which of the following statements are false?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-78c923c4-d570-4f9f-96c8-3d563b576db2.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Scientists still do not know why music probably helps language learning."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Piano lessons can heighten the brain''s response to changes in pitch."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Children who have attended kindergarten are more interested in music."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Mandarin is a tonal language, which is different from English."}, {"id": "E", "text": "Music lessons only benefit language learners who learn tonal languages."}]'::jsonb, '["C", "E"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Listen to the audio and select all correct options.', 'medium', 2, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcma-14000225', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcma', 'MCQ Multiple Answer', 'English Landscape Garden', 'Which of the following are mentioned as influences on the English landscape garden?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-2241bd36-ac56-4820-b8af-724df6fbd341.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Italian classical painting"}, {"id": "B", "text": "Gardens from classical Greece and Rome"}, {"id": "C", "text": "The Romantic Movement"}, {"id": "D", "text": "A person''s political affiliations"}, {"id": "E", "text": "The poet Alexander Pope"}]'::jsonb, '["A", "C", "E"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Listen to the audio and select all correct options.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcma-14000223', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcma', 'MCQ Multiple Answer', 'Rousseau''s Beliefs', 'Which of the following statements is true of Rousseau''s beliefs in The Social Contract?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-8199d608-dd68-43da-89c4-a4da0720e487.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Children''s emotions should be educated before their intellect."}, {"id": "B", "text": "People were far happier in a \"state of nature\" before civilization."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By forming societies, law and morality come into force."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Men form societies to better cope with the dangers in life."}, {"id": "E", "text": "Society has a corrupting influence on people."}]'::jsonb, '["C", "D"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Listen to the audio and select all correct options.', 'medium', 2, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcma-14000222', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcma', 'MCQ Multiple Answer', 'Children''s Education', 'Which of the following conditions need to be met by parents who want to have their children educated at home?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-be4ce24f-130f-4540-8816-7c8c81a8a590.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "They must keep a record of attendance."}, {"id": "B", "text": "They must ensure their child plays a sport."}, {"id": "C", "text": "They must provide regular assessments."}, {"id": "D", "text": "They must provide lesson plans."}, {"id": "E", "text": "They must provide book lists."}]'::jsonb, '["B", "D", "E"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Listen to the audio and select all correct options.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcma-14000221', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcma', 'MCQ Multiple Answer', 'Politics', 'Which of the following are suggested as reasons why contemporary writers on politics are less readable and relevant than the
ancient writers?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-f6926261-6c04-4bd2-b297-6c742e96c58a.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "They only write about institutions."}, {"id": "B", "text": "They ask largely irrelevant questions."}, {"id": "C", "text": "They tend to focus on only one aspect of political systems."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Being university-based forces them to specialize."}, {"id": "E", "text": "They follow the example of 191h century writers."}]'::jsonb, '["C", "D"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Listen to the audio and select all correct options.', 'medium', 2, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lfib-15000432', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-fib', 'Listening Fill in the Blanks', 'Work in Organization', 'You will hear a recording. Type the missing words in each blank.', 'In organizations where [[b1]] is encouraged, the exchange of knowledge, much of which is gained through environment, including the arrangement of shared spaces in which these experience, often takes place outside formal meetings. Employees, by [[b2]] ideas with colleagues from other departments, can develop a better understanding of problems that, on their own, they might find difficult to solve. The quality of the work [[b3]], including the arrangement of shared spaces in which these exchanges occur, is therefore important. Its effect on [[b4]], a measure of output in relation to the resources used, depends, however, on whether people can concentrate as well as communicate. Although frequent interaction can help groups produce more effective solutions, interruptions, particularly for those engaged in tasks requiring sustained attention, may reduce the quality of their work. The challenge for managers, then, is to optimize the use of space, so that opportunities for [[b5]] do not come at the expense of individual concentration.', 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/1656084c-0188-4f2f-9746-e1ab41a7350f.mp3', 'In organizations where teamwork is encouraged, the exchange of knowledge, much of which is gained through environment, including the arrangement of shared spaces in which these experience, often takes place outside formal meetings. Employees, by swapping ideas with colleagues from other departments, can develop a better understanding of problems that, on their own, they might find difficult to solve. The quality of the work environment, including the arrangement of shared spaces in which these exchanges occur, is therefore important. Its effect on productivity, a measure of output in relation to the resources used, depends, however, on whether people can concentrate as well as communicate. Although frequent interaction can help groups produce more effective solutions, interruptions, particularly for those engaged in tasks requiring sustained attention, may reduce the quality of their work. The challenge for managers, then, is to optimize the use of space, so that opportunities for collaboration do not come at the expense of individual concentration.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "b1", "correctAnswer": "teamwork"}, {"id": "b2", "correctAnswer": "swapping"}, {"id": "b3", "correctAnswer": "environment"}, {"id": "b4", "correctAnswer": "productivity"}, {"id": "b5", "correctAnswer": "collaboration"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Type the exact words heard in the audio.', 'medium', 5, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 120, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lfib-15000431', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-fib', 'Listening Fill in the Blanks', 'Sugar and Health', 'You will hear a recording. Type the missing words in each blank.', 'In Sri Lanka, as elsewhere, excess [[b1]], salt and fat in food and beverages are the primary culprits for the rise in the number of people that are overweight or [[b2]]. By ensuring clear and accurate nutritional information is provided on food and drink packaging, and by giving each product a green, orange or red label according to its sugar content, Sri Lanka''s government is helping [[b3]] understand risks and make healthier choices.', 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-533abfc3-2dd3-4084-8a45-a6721eed60a0.mp3', 'In Sri Lanka, as elsewhere, excess sugar, salt and fat in food and beverages are the primary culprits for the rise in the number of people that are overweight or obese. By ensuring clear and accurate nutritional information is provided on food and drink packaging, and by giving each product a green, orange or red label according to its sugar content, Sri Lanka''s government is helping consumers understand risks and make healthier choices.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "b1", "correctAnswer": "sugar"}, {"id": "b2", "correctAnswer": "obese"}, {"id": "b3", "correctAnswer": "consumers"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Type the exact words heard in the audio.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 120, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lfib-15000430', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-fib', 'Listening Fill in the Blanks', 'Building Responsibility', 'You will hear a recording. Type the missing words in each blank.', 'At school, the students [[b1]] that responsibilities can help build [[b2]] communities. The teacher reminded them that integrity means keeping [[b3]] even in small matters. One day, they made a discovery of ancient words in a library book, which [[b4]] the whole class. They realized that honest actions together with shared [[b5]] can shape a brighter future.', 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-bba821d6-f4e2-4003-845c-2ce3805e843d.mp3', 'At school, the students understood that responsibilities can help build strong communities. The teacher reminded them that integrity means keeping promises even in small matters. One day, they made a discovery of ancient words in a library book, which inspired the whole class. They realized that honest actions together with shared responsibilities can shape a brighter future.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "b1", "correctAnswer": "understood"}, {"id": "b2", "correctAnswer": "strong"}, {"id": "b3", "correctAnswer": "promises"}, {"id": "b4", "correctAnswer": "inspired"}, {"id": "b5", "correctAnswer": "responsibilities"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Type the exact words heard in the audio.', 'medium', 5, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 120, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lfib-15000429', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-fib', 'Listening Fill in the Blanks', 'Javelin Competition', 'You will hear a recording. Type the missing words in each blank.', 'The [[b1]] at the sports festival was the javelin competition. Athletes from all over the country came to participate. Many [[b2]] were excited to show their skills in [[b3]] the javelin as far as possible. They were organized into different [[b4]] to compete against each other. The biggest team, which had the most experienced members, took the lead. They [[b5]] the competition with an impressive throw.', 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-047dde46-9662-44e1-adf5-19dd301a8173.mp3', 'The biggest event at the sports festival was the javelin competition. Athletes from all over the country came to participate. Many people were excited to show their skills in throwing the javelin as far as possible. They were organized into different teams to compete against each other. The biggest team, which had the most experienced members, took the lead. They started the competition with an impressive throw.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "b1", "correctAnswer": "biggest event"}, {"id": "b2", "correctAnswer": "people"}, {"id": "b3", "correctAnswer": "throwing"}, {"id": "b4", "correctAnswer": "teams"}, {"id": "b5", "correctAnswer": "started"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Type the exact words heard in the audio.', 'medium', 5, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 120, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lfib-15000428', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-fib', 'Listening Fill in the Blanks', 'Local Farmers', 'You will hear a recording. Type the missing words in each blank.', 'Local farmers [[b1]] experiment with new methods to grow their crops more efficiently. They want to improve their harvests each season. Different [[b2]] of farming, such as organic or vertical farming, are becoming popular. Many [[b3]] now offer subscription services to deliver their produce directly to customers. They pack [[b4]] vegetables into a [[b5]] for families to enjoy weekly. This ensures people have access to healthy food.', 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-babcb48b-ad68-4e7f-9291-364e413a61d9.mp3', 'Local farmers frequently experiment with new methods to grow their crops more efficiently. They want to improve their harvests each season. Different styles of farming, such as organic or vertical farming, are becoming popular. Many farms now offer subscription services to deliver their produce directly to customers. They pack fresh vegetables into a box for families to enjoy weekly. This ensures people have access to healthy food.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "b1", "correctAnswer": "frequently"}, {"id": "b2", "correctAnswer": "styles"}, {"id": "b3", "correctAnswer": "farms"}, {"id": "b4", "correctAnswer": "fresh"}, {"id": "b5", "correctAnswer": "box"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Type the exact words heard in the audio.', 'medium', 5, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 7, 120, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-hcs-19000162', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-correct-summary', 'Highlight Correct Summary', 'Sodium', 'You will hear a recording. Click on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-111ab582-3c4a-4d59-8430-5831703d9b68.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Sodium is harmful to the human body and should be eliminated entirely, as the kidney cannot regulate it effectively."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Sodium levels never change in the body, so no regulation is needed."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Sodium is stored only in the bones, and its balance is controlled by the lungs rather than the kidneys."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Sodium is an essential mineral, and the kidney uses filtration, reabsorption, and hormones to maintain body sodium balance."}]'::jsonb, '["D"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Click on the paragraph that best summarizes the audio.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 10, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-hcs-19000160', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-correct-summary', 'Highlight Correct Summary', 'Mountains', 'You will hear a recording. Click on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-b23d06dd-5f59-4be5-8905-0e834783d08f.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Geologists are trying to build up a mountain that stretches between New York and Chicago, which will soar over 45km. This has been warned by experts that the support of such mountain may be damaged by winds and glaciers."}, {"id": "B", "text": "For any conical mountain on the Earth, its height is limited by various factors. The factors include the Earth''s mantle, collision of tectonic plates and erosion, so the tallest mountains are not likely to grow much higher."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Mount Everest may grow in the future, because it won''t sink lower into the Earth''s hot interior like other mountains do. Another reason is that it hasn''t reached the height limit of 15km yet."}, {"id": "D", "text": "The Earth''s crust is made up of continental plates that float in the rock of its mantle. This can result in earthquakes, which may force the highest mountains to collapse, according to a research."}]'::jsonb, '["B"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Click on the paragraph that best summarizes the audio.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 10, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-hcs-19000159', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-correct-summary', 'Highlight Correct Summary', 'DNA Model', 'You will hear a recording. Click on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-e7013a47-e870-436c-a441-501a60e89be3.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "The proposed model uses Mobius weight functions to unify topological and sequence-dependent torsional characteristics in DNA."}, {"id": "B", "text": "The model treats DNA as a flat, untwisted ribbon and uses the Mobius function solely for visual strand orientation mapping."}, {"id": "C", "text": "The Mobius weight energy function models DNA purely as a bending rod and does not account for torsional topology or sequence variability."}, {"id": "D", "text": "The Mobius weight function focuses exclusively on electronic base-pair interactions, ignoring large-scale mechanical properties."}]'::jsonb, '["A"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Click on the paragraph that best summarizes the audio.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 10, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-hcs-19000158', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-correct-summary', 'Highlight Correct Summary', 'Genealogy', 'You will hear a recording. Click on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-10ebedc0-7f15-4591-9c7d-fed103cae286.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "The study of family history began hundreds of years ago in North Africa in order to establish such things as ownership of property. It rapidly became a common practice in many cultures because inheritance played such an important role in society and government."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Research into family history by ordinary people only started to become far more widespread in the early nineteenth century. Prior to that time, it was chiefly rich. important and powerful families who had an interest and involvement in this type of activity."}, {"id": "C", "text": "All social classes of the general population have always been interested in recording their family history. but genealogy became really popular in the early nineteenth century due to the publication of a book concerning the methodology of determining family history."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Originally. tracing family history was only used in order to establish the origins of prosperous and powerful families. However. by the middle of the twentieth century. ordinary people were also starting to show an interest in researching their family background too."}]'::jsonb, '["D"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Click on the paragraph that best summarizes the audio.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 10, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-hcs-19000157', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-correct-summary', 'Highlight Correct Summary', 'Early Humans', 'You will hear a recording. Click on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-11572148-7486-42ef-96d2-a0f43949a02a.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Recent findings have convinced the anthropological community that previous conclusions from research done over many decades were correct in estimating when early humans started to use fire, although this research was incorrect in its findings about what fire was used for."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Anthropologists have disagreed for some time regarding when and how fire was first used in prehistoric times. Recent findings have now managed to finally persuade them that it was used before they thought and the principle use of fire was for cooking rather than any other purpose."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Scientists believe they are now closer to finding an answer to the question of when humans first started to use fire, and it is much earlier than had been thought. Nevertheless, there is still some disagreement among researchers around what early humans used the fire for."}, {"id": "D", "text": "There has been much discussion by anthropologists about when humans started to use fires. As a result of a recent discovery it is thought that they started to make fires 300,000 years ago, but the reason they made them is still not clear."}]'::jsonb, '["C"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Click on the paragraph that best summarizes the audio.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 10, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcsa-17000219', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcsa', 'MCQ Single Answer', 'Literary Genres', 'Which of the following is not mentioned as being a type of genre fiction?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-8339547f-74e8-4ee7-9de3-d9588b569e54.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "mainstream"}, {"id": "B", "text": "gothic"}, {"id": "C", "text": "fantasy"}, {"id": "D", "text": "romance"}]'::jsonb, '["A"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single correct answer based on the recording.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 5, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcsa-17000218', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcsa', 'MCQ Single Answer', 'Narcissism', 'What is the speaker''s attitude to the report on narcissism?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-a16e4a01-013d-4258-b27a-d3ac2da6efea.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "He is angered by it."}, {"id": "B", "text": "He is skeptical of it."}, {"id": "C", "text": "He is amused by it."}, {"id": "D", "text": "He doesn''t believe any of it is true."}]'::jsonb, '["B"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single correct answer based on the recording.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 5, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcsa-17000217', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcsa', 'MCQ Single Answer', 'Reasonable Force', 'Which of the following is true according to the speaker?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-d7ffbc73-3bb4-4809-be76-00bab86d6eff.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "The concept of reasonable force is very clearly defined."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Your use of force may be judged on how strong you are compared to the other person."}, {"id": "C", "text": "If you hit someone first, you cannot then claim self-defence."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Courts do not expect ordinary people to react rationally."}]'::jsonb, '["B"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single correct answer based on the recording.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 5, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
    ('pte-alfa-lmcsa-17000216', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcsa', 'MCQ Single Answer', 'Randall Jarrell', 'In the speaker''s opinion, which of the following is true of editors who are also novelists?', NULL, 'https://cdn-alfastorage.alfapte.com/question-files/audio-19b84a2c-3eb7-41d5-a4c3-3d48e5c04baf.mp3', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "They are sympathetic to the difficult lives authors lead."}, {"id": "B", "text": "They are always able to see the novel from the author''s point of view."}, {"id": "C", "text": "They find it difficult to see the author''s real intentions."}, {"id": "D", "text": "They may try to re-shape the novelist''s work in their own way."}]'::jsonb, '["D"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Select the single correct answer based on the recording.', 'medium', 1, ARRAY['PTE', 'Alfa PTE', 'Listening']::text[], TRUE, 5, 90, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
